            <div xml:id="d639">

                <pb facs="0609" n="597" sameAs="frus:frus1943v04/pg597"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">121.5767/6: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Minister in Iran</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Dreyfus</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Tehran</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1943-09-02T09:00:00+03:25">September 2,
                            1943—9 a.m.</date>
                        <lb/> [Received 10:58 a.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>910. Department’s 441, August 26. Both Gunter and Millspaugh approve the amended
                    wording suggested by Treasury. The latter is requesting Foreign Office to
                    telegraph instructions to Iranian Minister in Wellington [<hi
                        rendition="#italic">Washington?</hi>] to proceed with discussions and is
                    asking Government to submit proposed bill to Medjliss.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Dreyfus</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
